tion/_pls.py:PLSRegression` to get the full content if needed.\n\nFound class `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSCanonical`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass PLSCanonical(_PLS):\n\n    # This implementation provides the same results that the \"plspm\" package\n    # provided in the R language (R-project), using the function plsca(X, Y).\n    # Results are equal or collinear with the function\n    # ``pls(..., mode = \"canonical\")`` of the \"mixOmics\" package. The\n    # difference relies in the fact that mixOmics implementation does not\n    # exactly implement the Wold algorithm since it does not normalize\n    # y_weights to one.\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        n_components=2,\n        *,\n        scale=True,\n        algorithm=\"nipals\",\n        max_iter=500,\n        tol=1e-06,\n        copy=True,\n    ):\n\n```\nHint: Search `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSCanonical` to get the full content if needed.\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/validation.py:check_non_negative`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1336 | def check_non_negative(X, whom):\n1337 |     \"\"\"\n1338 |     Check if there is any negative value in an array.\n1339 | \n1340 |     Parameters\n1341 |     ----------\n1342 |     X : {array-like, sparse matrix}\n1343 |         Input data.\n1344 | \n1345 |     whom : str\n1346 |         Who passed X to this function.\n1347 |     \"\"\"\n1348 |     # avoid X.min() on sparse matrix since it also sorts the indices\n1349 |     if sp.issparse(X):\n1350 |         if X.format in [\"lil\", \"dok\"]:\n1351 |             X = X.tocsr()\n1352 |         if X.data.size == 0:\n1353 |             X_min = 0\n1354 |         else:\n1355 |             X_min = X.data.min()\n1356 |     else:\n1357 |         X_min = X.min()\n1358 | \n1359 |     if X_min < 0:\n1360 |         raise ValueError(\"Negative values in data passed to %s\" % whom)\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/validation.py:_generate_get_feature_names_out`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1918 | def _generate_get_feature_names_out(estimator, n_features_out, input_features=None):\n1919 |     \"\"\"Generate feature names out for estimator using the estimator name as the prefix.\n1920 | \n1921 |     The input_feature names are validated but not used. This function is useful\n1922 |     for estimators that generate their own names based on `n_features_out`, i.e. PCA.\n1923 | \n1924 |     Parameters\n1925 |     ----------\n1926 |     estimator : estimator instance\n1927 |         Estimator producing output feature names.\n1928 | \n1929 |     n_feature_out : int\n1930 |         Number of feature names out.\n1931 | \n1932 |     input_features : array-like of str or None, default=None\n1933 |         Only used to validate feature names with `estimator.feature_names_in_`.\n1934 | \n1935 |     Returns\n1936 |     -------\n1937 |     feature_names_in : ndarray of str or `None`\n1938 |         Feature names in.\n1939 |     \"\"\"\n1940 |     _check_feature_names_in(estimator, input_features, generate_names=False)\n1941 |     estimator_name = estimator.__class__.__name__.lower()\n1942 |     return np.asarray(\n1943 |         [f\"{estimator_name}{i}\" for i in range(n_features_out)], dtype=object\n1944 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/neighbors/_lof.py:LocalOutlierFactor.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n258 | def fit(self, X, y=None):\n259 |         \"\"\"Fit the local outlier factor detector from the training dataset.\n260 | \n261 |         Parameters\n262 |         ----------\n263 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features) or \\\n264 |                 (n_samples, n_samples) if metric='precomputed'\n265 |             Training data.\n266 | \n267 |         y : Ignored\n268 |             Not used, present for API consistency by convention.\n269 | \n270 |         Returns\n271 |         -------\n272 |         self : LocalOutlierFactor\n273 |             The fitted local outlier factor detector.\n274 |         \"\"\"\n275 |         self._fit(X)\n276 | \n277 |         if self.contamination != \"auto\":\n278 |             if not (0.0 < self.contamination <= 0.5):\n279 |                 raise ValueError(\n280 |                     \"contamination must be in (0, 0.5], got: %f\" % self.contamination\n281 |                 )\n282 | \n283 |         n_samples = self.n_samples_fit_\n284 |         if self.n_neighbors > n_samples:\n285 |             warnings.warn(\n286 |                 \"n_neighbors (%s) is greater than the \"\n287 |                 \"total number of samples (%s). n_neighbors \"\n288 |                 \"will be set to (n_samples - 1) for estimation.\"\n289 |                 % (self.n_neighbors, n_samples)\n290 |             )\n291 |         self.n_neighbors_ = max(1, min(self.n_neighbors, n_samples - 1))\n292 | \n293 |         self._distances_fit_X_, _neighbors_indices_fit_X_ = self.kneighbors(\n294 |             n_neighbors=self.n_neighbors_\n295 |         )\n296 | \n297 |         self._lrd = self._local_reachability_density(\n298 |             self._distances_fit_X_, _neighbors_indices_fit_X_\n299 |         )\n300 | \n301 |         # Compute lof score over training samples to define offset_:\n302 |         lrd_ratios_array = (\n303 |             self._lrd[_neighbors_indices_fit_X_] / self._lrd[:, np.newaxis]\n304 |         )\n305 | \n306 |         self.negative_outlier_factor_ = -np.mean(lrd_ratios_array, axis=1)\n307 | \n308 |         if self.contamination == \"auto\":\n309 |             # inliers score around -1 (the higher, the less abnormal).\n310 |             self.offset_ = -1.5\n311 |         else:\n312 |             self.offset_ = np.percentile(\n313 |                 self.negative_outlier_factor_, 100.0 * self.contamination\n314 |             )\n315 | \n316 |         return self\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSRegression.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n634 | def fit(self, X, Y):\n635 |         \"\"\"Fit model to data.\n636 | \n637 |         Parameters\n638 |         ----------\n639 |         X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n640 |             Training vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n641 |             `n_features` is the number of predictors.\n642 | \n643 |         Y : array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_targets)\n644 |             Target vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n645 |             `n_targets` is the number of response variables.\n646 | \n647 |         Returns\n648 |         -------\n649 |         self : object\n650 |             Fitted model.\n651 |         \"\"\"\n652 |         super().fit(X, Y)\n653 |         # expose the fitted attributes `x_scores_` and `y_scores_`\n654 |         self.x_scores_ = self._x_scores\n655 |         self.y_scores_ = self._y_scores\n656 |         return self\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/utils/validation.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/utils/validation.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"NMF\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/decomposition/_nmf.py:NMF`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `NMF`.\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass NMF(_ClassNamePrefixFeaturesOutMixin, TransformerMixin, BaseEstimator):\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        n_components=None,\n        *,\n        init=None,\n        solver=\"cd\",\n        beta_loss=\"frobenius\",\n        tol=1e-4,\n        max_iter=200,\n        random_state=None,\n        alpha=\"deprecated\",\n        alpha_W=0.0,\n        alpha_H=\"same\",\n        l1_ratio=0.0,\n        verbose=0,\n        shuffle=False,\n        regularization=\"depreca