|     Parameters\n267 |     ----------\n268 |     estimator : estimator object\n269 |         The estimator for which to get the default tags.\n270 | \n271 |     Returns\n272 |     -------\n273 |     tags : Tags\n274 |         The default tags for the estimator.\n275 |     \"\"\"\n276 |     est_is_classifier = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"classifier\"\n277 |     est_is_regressor = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"regressor\"\n278 |     target_required = est_is_classifier or est_is_regressor\n279 | \n280 |     return Tags(\n281 |         estimator_type=getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None),\n282 |         target_tags=TargetTags(required=target_required),\n283 |         transformer_tags=(\n284 |             TransformerTags()\n285 |             if hasattr(estimator, \"transform\") or hasattr(estimator, \"fit_transform\")\n286 |             else None\n287 |         ),\n288 |         classifier_tags=ClassifierTags() if est_is_classifier else None,\n289 |         regressor_tags=RegressorTags() if est_is_regressor else None,\n290 |     )\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"TargetTags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:TargetTags`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `TargetTags`.\n```\n 74 | class TargetTags:\n 75 |     \"\"\"Tags for the target data.\n 76 | \n 77 |     Parameters\n 78 |     ----------\n 79 |     required : bool\n 80 |         Whether the estimator requires y to be passed to `fit`,\n 81 |         `fit_predict` or `fit_transform` methods. The tag is ``True``\n 82 |         for estimators inheriting from `~sklearn.base.RegressorMixin`\n 83 |         and `~sklearn.base.ClassifierMixin`.\n 84 | \n 85 |     one_d_labels : bool, default=False\n 86 |         Whether the input is a 1D labels (y).\n 87 | \n 88 |     two_d_labels : bool, default=False\n 89 |         Whether the input is a 2D labels (y).\n 90 | \n 91 |     positive_only : bool, default=False\n 92 |         Whether the estimator requires a positive y (only applicable\n 93 |         for regression).\n 94 | \n 95 |     multi_output : bool, default=False\n 96 |         Whether a regressor supports multi-target outputs or a classifier supports\n 97 |         multi-class multi-output.\n 98 | \n 99 |     single_output : bool, default=True\n100 |         Whether the target can be single-output. This can be ``False`` if the\n101 |         estimator supports only multi-output cases.\n102 |     \"\"\"\n103 | \n104 |     required: bool\n105 |     one_d_labels: bool = False\n106 |     two_d_labels: bool = False\n107 |     positive_only: bool = False\n108 |     multi_output: bool = False\n109 |     single_output: bool = True\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"ClassifierTags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:ClassifierTags`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n133 | class ClassifierTags:\n134 |     \"\"\"Tags for the classifier.\n135 | \n136 |     Parameters\n137 |     ----------\n138 |     poor_score : bool, default=False\n139 |         Whether the estimator fails to provide a \"reasonable\" test-set\n140 |         score, which currently for classification is an accuracy of\n141 |         0.83 on ``make_blobs(n_samples=300, random_state=0)``. The\n142 |         datasets and values are based on current estimators in scikit-learn\n143 |         and might be replaced by something more systematic.\n144 | \n145 |     multi_class : bool, default=True\n146 |         Whether the classifier can handle multi-class\n147 |         classification. Note that all classifiers support binary\n148 |         classification. Therefore this flag indicates whether the\n149 |         classifier is a binary-classifier-only or not.\n150 | \n151 |     multi_label : bool, default=False\n152 |         Whether the classifier supports multi-label output.\n153 |     \"\"\"\n154 | \n155 |     poor_score: bool = False\n156 |     multi_class: bool = True\n157 |     multi_label: bool = False\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/__init__.py:__getattr__`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n106 | def __getattr__(name):\n107 |     if name == \"IS_PYPY\":\n108 |         warnings.warn(\n109 |             \"IS_PYPY is deprecated and will be removed in 1.7.\",\n110 |             FutureWarning,\n111 |         )\n112 |         return platform.python_implementation() == \"PyPy\"\n113 |     raise AttributeError(f\"module {__name__} has no attribute {name}\")\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"ClassifierTags\", \"Tags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:Tags`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n183 | class Tags:\n184 |     \"\"\"Tags for the estimator.\n185 | \n186 |     See :ref:`estimator_tags` for more information.\n187 | \n188 |     Parameters\n189 |     ----------\n190 |     estimator_type : str or None\n191 |         The type of the estimator. Can be one of:\n192 |         - \"classifier\"\n193 |         - \"regressor\"\n194 |         - \"transformer\"\n195 |         - \"clusterer\"\n196 |         - \"outlier_detector\"\n197 |         - \"density_estimator\"\n198 | \n199 |     target_tags : :class:`TargetTags`\n200 |         The target(y) tags.\n201 | \n202 |     transformer_tags : :class:`TransformerTags` or None\n203 |         The transformer tags.\n204 | \n205 |     classifier_tags : :class:`ClassifierTags` or None\n206 |         The classifier tags.\n207 | \n208 |     regressor_tags : :class:`RegressorTags` or None\n209 |         The regressor tags.\n210 | \n211 |     array_api_support : bool, default=False\n212 |         Whether the estimator supports Array API compatible inputs.\n213 | \n214 |     no_validation : bool, default=False\n215 |         Whether the estimator skips input-validation. This is only meant for\n216 |         stateless and dummy transformers!\n217 | \n218 |     non_deterministic : bool, default=False\n219 |         Whether the estimator is not deterministic given a fixed ``random_state``.\n220 | \n221 |     requires_fit : bool, default=True\n222 |         Whether the estimator requires to be fitted before calling one of\n223 |         `transform`, `predict`, `predict_proba`, or `decision_function`.\n224 | \n225 |     _skip_test : bool, default=False\n226 |         Whether to skip common tests entirely. Don't use this unless\n227 |         you have a *very good* reason.\n228 | \n229 |     input_tags : :class:`InputTags`\n230 |         The input data(X) tags.\n231 |     \"\"\"\n232 | \n233 |     estimator_type: str | None\n234 |     target_tags: TargetTags\n235 |     transformer_tags: TransformerTags | None = None\n236 |     classifier_tags: ClassifierTags | None = None\n237 |     regressor_tags: RegressorTags | None = None\n238 |     array_api_support: bool = False\n239 |     no_validation: bool = False\n240 |     non_deterministic: bool = False\n241 |     requires_fit: bool = True\n242 |     _skip_test: bool = False\n243 |     input_tags: InputTags = field(default_factory=InputTags)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"RegressorTags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:RegressorTags`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `RegressorTags`.\n```\n161 | class RegressorTags:\n162 |     \"\"\"Tags for the regressor.\n163 | \n164 |     Parameters\n165 |     ----------\n166 |     poor_score : bool, default=False\n167 |         Whether the estimator fails to provide a \"reasonable\" test-set\n168 |         score, which currently for regression is an R2 of 0.5 on\n169 |         ``make_regression(n_samples=200, n_features=10,\n170 |         n_informative=1, bias=5.0, noise=20, random_state=42)``. The\n171 |         dataset and values are based on current estimators in scikit-learn\n172 |         and might be replaced by something more systematic.\n173 | \n174 |     multi_label : bool, default=False\n175 |         Whether the regressor supports multilabel output.\n176 |     \"\"\"\n177 | \n178 |     poor_score: bool = False\n179 |     multi_label: bool = False\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"TransformerTags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:TransformerTags`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `TransformerTags`.\n```\n113 | class TransformerTags:\n114 |     \"\"\"Tags for the transformer.\n115 | \n116 |     Parameters\n117 |     ----------\n118 |     preserves_dtype : list[str], default=[\"float64\"]\n119 |         Applies only on transformers. It corresponds to the data types\n120 |         which will be preserved such that `X_trans.dtype` is the same\n121 |         as `X.dtype` after calling `transformer.transform(X)`. If this\n122 |         list is empty, then the transformer is not expected to\n123 |         preserve the data type. The first value in the list is\n124 |         considered as the default data type, corresponding to the data\n125 |         type of the output when the input data type is not going to be\n126 |         preserved.\n127 |     \"\"\"\n128 | \n129 |     preserves_dtype: list[str] = field(default_factory=lambda: [\"float64\"])\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, I can now provide the locations that need to be modified to implement the requested feature. Here's the output in the requested format:\n\n```\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 247\nline: 293-334\nfunction: get_tags\n\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 247-290\nfunction: default_tags\n\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py\nline: 4447\nline: 4453-4466\nfunction: check_estimator_tags_renamed\n\nsklearn/base.py\nline: 560\nfunction: BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__\n\nsklearn/utils/__init__.py\nline: 106-112\nfunction: __getattr__\n```\n\nThese locations are ordered by importance, with the most critical files and functions listed first. The key modifications needed are:\n\n1. `sklearn/utils/_tags.py`: This is the main file that needs changes to implement the tag conversion functionality. Specifically:\n   - The `get_tags` function need