: {'property', 'method'}\n166 |     overwrite : bool, default False\n167 |        Overwrite the method/property in the target class if it exists.\n168 |     accessor_mapping: Callable, default lambda x: x\n169 |         Callable to map the delegate's function to the cls' function.\n170 |     raise_on_missing: bool, default True\n171 |         Raise if an accessor does not exist on delegate.\n172 |         False skips the missing accessor.\n173 | \n174 |     Returns\n175 |     -------\n176 |     callable\n177 |         A class decorator.\n178 | \n179 |     Examples\n180 |     --------\n181 |     @delegate_names(Categorical, [\"categories\", \"ordered\"], \"property\")\n182 |     class CategoricalAccessor(PandasDelegate):\n183 |         [...]\n184 |     \"\"\"\n185 | \n186 |     def add_delegate_accessors(cls):\n187 |         cls._add_delegate_accessors(\n188 |             delegate,\n189 |             accessors,\n190 |             typ,\n191 |             overwrite=overwrite,\n192 |             accessor_mapping=accessor_mapping,\n193 |             raise_on_missing=raise_on_missing,\n194 |         )\n195 |         return cls\n196 | \n197 |     return add_delegate_accessors\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"AttributeError\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/errors/__init__.py:AttributeConflictWarning`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n648 | class AttributeConflictWarning(Warning):\n649 |     \"\"\"\n650 |     Warning raised when index attributes conflict when using HDFStore.\n651 | \n652 |     Occurs when attempting to append an index with a different\n653 |     name than the existing index on an HDFStore or attempting to append an index with a\n654 |     different frequency than the existing index on an HDFStore.\n655 | \n656 |     Examples\n657 |     --------\n658 |     >>> idx1 = pd.Index([\"a\", \"b\"], name=\"name1\")\n659 |     >>> df1 = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2], [3, 4]], index=idx1)\n660 |     >>> df1.to_hdf(\"file\", \"data\", \